              <div
                id="platform-guide"
              />
              <section
                class="map2x-guide-section"
              >
                <div
                  class="map2x-guide-section__inner"
                >
                  <div
                    class="map2x-eyebrow map2x-eyebrow--accent map2x-guide-section__eyebrow"
                  >
                    — Why
                  </div>
                  <h2
                    class="map2x-guide-section__title"
                  >
                    It started as a digital pedalboard.
                  </h2>
                  <div
                    class="map2x-prose"
                  >
                    <p>
                      Most modern bands already operate in a digital signal chain. Guitar modelers, digital mixers, drum triggers, MIDI controllers — every modern capture of a musical instrument converts to digital almost immediately.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                      So, with a lot of help from AI, MAP2 extends that idea to its logical conclusion: a centralised digital audio backbone with sufficient I/O to handle the entire band simultaneously. Microphones, line inputs, MIDI keyboards, drum triggers, amp modelers — everything.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                      No redundant interfaces. No repeated A/D and D/A conversions. No audio leaving and re-entering the digital domain. The signal path remains coherent, clocked and lossless from input to archive. That's technically optimal.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </section>
              <section
                class="map2x-guide-section"
                id="modes"
              >
                <div
                  class="map2x-guide-section__inner"
                >
                  <div
                    class="map2x-eyebrow map2x-eyebrow--accent map2x-guide-section__eyebrow"
                  >
                    — Operating modes
                  </div>
                  <h2
                    class="map2x-guide-section__title"
                  >
                    Three modes, one platform.
                  </h2>
                  <p
                    class="map2x-guide-section__sub"
                  >
                    Each MAP2 node boots into one of three roles. Same image, different responsibilities.
                  </p>
                  <div
                    class="map2x-panel"
                  >
                    <div
                      class="map2x-kv-head"
                    >
                      <div
                        class="map2x-kv-head__cell"
                      >
                        Mode
                      </div>
                      <div
                        class="map2x-kv-head__cell"
                      >
                        Latency
                      </div>
                      <div
                        class="map2x-kv-head__cell"
                      >
                        Description
                      </div>
                    </div>
                    <div
                      class="map2x-kv-row"
                    >
                      <div
                        class="map2x-kv-row__cell map2x-kv-row__cell--head"
                      >
                        Audio
                      </div>
                      <div
                        class="map2x-kv-row__cell"
                      >
                        2.67 ms theoretical floor; 4–7 ms measured
                      </div>
                      <div
                        class="map2x-kv-row__cell"
                      >
                        Dedicated processing on isolated CPU cores. No web UI.
                      </div>
                    </div>
                    <div
                      class="map2x-kv-row"
                    >
                      <div
                        class="map2x-kv-row__cell map2x-kv-row__cell--head"
                      >
                        All-in-One
                      </div>
                      <div
                        class="map2x-kv-row__cell"
                      >
                        4–7 ms realistic today
                      </div>
                      <div
                        class="map2x-kv-row__cell"
                      >
                        Audio processing + web dashboard + management on one node.
                      </div>
                    </div>
                    <div
                      class="map2x-kv-row is-last"
                    >
                      <div
                        class="map2x-kv-row__cell map2x-kv-row__cell--head"
                      >
                        Management
                      </div>
                      <div
                        class="map2x-kv-row__cell"
                      >
                        N/A
                      </div>
                      <div
                        class="map2x-kv-row__cell"
                      >
                        Control-only node for cluster administration.
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </section>
              <section
                class="map2x-guide-section"
                id="signal-chain"
              >
                <div
                  class="map2x-guide-section__inner"
                >
                  <div
                    class="map2x-eyebrow map2x-eyebrow--accent map2x-guide-section__eyebrow"
                  >
                    — Signal chain
                  </div>
                  <h2
                    class="map2x-guide-section__title"
                  >
                    Input to archive, in nine stages.
                  </h2>
                  <div
                    class="map2x-panel"
                  >
                    <div
                      class="map2x-strip"
                    >
                      <div
                        class="map2x-mono map2x-strip__title"
                      >
                        Signal Chain
                      </div>
                      <button
                        class="map2x-ghost-btn"
                        type="button"
                      >
                        Copy
                      </button>
                    </div>
                    <pre
                      class="map2x-code"
                    >
                      Input → NAM (Neural Amp) → Modulation (11 types) → Cabinet IR → EQ →
Gate → Compressor → Limiter → Reverb IR → Output
                    </pre>
                  </div>
                  <p
                    class="map2x-guide-section__hint"
                  >
                    All processing runs on isolated CPU cores with
                     
                    <span
                      class="map2x-mono"
                    >
                      SCHED_FIFO
                    </span>
                     real-time priority, PipeWire/JACK audio transport, and configurable buffer sizes down to 64 samples at 48 kHz.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </section>
